cated 3x at 15% for 7 seconds. Lysates were cleared at 13,000g for 10min at 4°C and protein concentrations were quantified using 600nM Pierce Assay Kit with Detergent Compatibility Reagent (ThermoFisher, #22662). Streptavidin magnetic beads (ThermoFisher, #88816) were washed 2x with RIPA buffer and 100uL washed beads were added per sample. Binding was allowed to proceed overnight at 4°C with rocking. Beads were collected on a magnetic rack and the following wash steps were performed at 4°C: 3x wash with RIPA buffer (5min each), 1x wash with 1M KCL (2min), 1x wash with Na2CO2 (2min),  and 2x with 50mM Tris-HCl [pH=8.0] (5min). Beads were resuspended in 200ul Digestion buffer (2M urea in 50mM Tris pH=8.0). Samples were reduced by adding 5mM TCEP and incubated at 37°C for 30min with orbital shaking at 1000rpm. Samples were alkylated with iodoacetamide at 5mM at room temperature, covered from light with orbital shaking at 1000rpm. The reaction was quenched with addition of 5mM DTT. Biotinylated proteins were digested with addition of 0.8ug mass spectrometry grade Trypsin (Promega, #V5111) overnight at 37°C with orbital shaking at 1000rpm. The following morning, an additional 0.4ug trypsin was added and incubated for 2hrs at 37°C with shaking. Samples were acidified with 0.5% TFA and desalted using C18 96-well plate format (Higgins Analytical, #96WR-20mg-W182).   APEX-labeled samples were acquired on a Bruker TimsTOFpro interfaced with an Ultimate3000 UHPLC. Peptides were resuspended in 0.1% FA and were separated using a 60 minutes linear gradient. Following loading, the percentage of B (80% ACN in 0.1% FA) was increased from 2% to 26% in 49\u2009min and then to 90% remaining time. The peptides were separated on a PepSep column (15\u2009cm, 150\u2009mm iid, 1.9\u2009μm beads size). The mass spectrometer was operated in positive mode using DIA-PASEF acquisition.41  The mass range was set at 100-1700m/z with 10 scans between 0.7 Vs/cm2 and 1.4 Vs/cm2. 2 ms and 100 ms were 